      description: "Fenoldopam is a rapid IV D1-receptor agonist that lowers blood pressure by dilating systemic and renal arteries. Unlike dopamine, it does not rely on alpha or beta stimulation; the price of fast afterload reduction is reflex tachycardia, headache/flushing, hypotension, hypokalemia, and increased intraocular pressure.",
