      description: "Cangrelor is an IV, direct, reversible P2Y12 inhibitor with near-immediate platelet inhibition and rapid offset after the infusion stops. That makes it useful during PCI when oral absorption or timing is unreliable, but bleeding and correct transition to an oral P2Y12 drug are the entire nursing safety story.",
      mechanism: "Cangrelor directly and reversibly blocks platelet P2Y12 ADP receptors, preventing ADP-driven activation of glycoprotein IIb/IIIa and platelet aggregation. It does not require hepatic activation, and platelet function begins recovering quickly after discontinuation.",
